# Edge AI Based Smart EV Charging Station Optimizer

An IoT-enabled smart EV charging station prototype using ESP32, Edge AI,
MQTT, and ThingsBoard for real-time monitoring and intelligent charging control.

## Project Overview

This project simulates a smart EV charging bay that can monitor electrical
parameters, detect charging conditions, make local charging decisions, and
send telemetry to a cloud dashboard.

The ESP32 performs edge-side decision making and communicates with ThingsBoard
using MQTT.

## Key Features

- Real-time voltage monitoring
- Real-time current monitoring
- Power calculation
- Energy consumption tracking
- Temperature monitoring using DHT22
- EV plug-in / plug-out detection
- Automatic charging control
- Overcurrent protection
- Charging throttling
- AI-based EV arrival probability prediction
- AI-based charging duration prediction
- MQTT telemetry
- ThingsBoard dashboard
- Remote relay control using RPC
- Manual charging override
- Real-time alerts and status monitoring

## Hardware

- ESP32 DevKit
- 2 × Potentiometers for simulated voltage/current inputs
- DHT22 temperature sensor
- Push buttons for EV plug-in and plug-out simulation
- Relay output
- Red, yellow and green LEDs
- Resistors

The hardware is simulated using Wokwi.

## Software & Technologies

- C++
- Arduino Framework
- ESP32
- PlatformIO
- Wokwi
- MQTT
- ThingsBoard
- Edge AI
- ArduinoJson
- DHT22

## System Architecture

```text
Sensors / User Inputs
        |
        v
      ESP32
        |
        +--> Sensor Processing
        |
        +--> Edge AI Prediction
        |
        +--> Charging Optimization
        |
        +--> Relay / LED Control
        |
        v
       MQTT
        |
        v
   ThingsBoard Cloud
        |
        +--> Real-time Dashboard
        +--> Telemetry
        +--> Alerts
        +--> RPC Control